speechtext:
Well, I will ask my colleague the Minister of Public Works to move:
That Bill C-95, an act to amend the Income Tax Act, be amended as follows:
1.	by striking out the expression "ownership and control" appearing in the heading immediately preceding section 105D of the Income Tax Act as set out in clause 22 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";
2.	by striking out the expression "ownership and control" in line 22 on page 18 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";
3.	by striking out the expression "ownership and control" in lines 35 and 36 on page 18 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";
4.	by striking out the expression "ownership or control" in lines 26 and 27 on page 20 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";
5.	by striking out the expression "ownership and control" in line 39 on page 20 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";
6.	by striking out the expression "ownership and control" in line 42 on page 20 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";
7.	by striking out the expression "ownership and control" in line 5 on page 25 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";
8.	by striking out the expression "ownership and control" in lines 40 and 41 on page 26 thereof and substituting therefor the expression "ownership";

At this moment, I will be content to use the word "supposed", in the light of what has happened in this house recently.
I want to read into the record a resolution passed by the representatives of the Northwest Territories. These are the people elected by the people of the Northwest Territories

Private Bills
to represent them in the government of the Northwest Territories. This is what they said:
Whereas the council of the Northwest Territories has reviewed the bill to amend the Northwest Territories Act in order to create the territory of Mackenzie and the bill to create the territory of Nunassiaq, as given first reading in the House of Commons on July 8, 1963;
And whereas the bills embody the provisions requested in the resolution passed by the council of the Northwest Territories in its session in Ottawa in January, 1962, after more than two years of consideration and study, and are satisfactory in all respects to the council;
And whereas there will be great inconvenience if the bills are not passed by November 7, 1963, at the latest, with effective date for the establishment of the new territories from April 1, 1964, as provided in the bills;
Now, therefore, the council of the Northwest Territories respectfully expresses its appreciation for the submission of legislation to carry out the action that it has requested in the interests of the progress and development of government in the territories.
Then, my hon. friend from the Northwest Territories, which he says he represents, is quite prepared to obstruct in every respect-
